WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.890
Link building usually eats a whole team: finding sites,

2
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:08.130
writing to webmasters, negotiating,

3
00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:10.750
paying, and checking the links.

4
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:11.950
In production,

5
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.840
this platform let one operator do the work of five people.

6
00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:21.460
This is a demo copy — the sites and people are invented.

7
00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:25.580
It covers the whole cycle.

8
00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:31.230
It takes a competitor's backlinks and checks every site —

9
00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:34.270
quality, traffic, spam, topic.

10
00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:38.480
The ones that pass become donors, with a grade.

11
00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:43.150
Outreach goes out in safe batches.

12
00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:46.210
Every reply lands in one inbox,

13
00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:51.030
where you see the deal stage and who owns the thread.

14
00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:55.310
The AI writes a draft; a person sends it.

15
00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:01.150
This one never went out.

16
00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:04.360
The webmaster said the budget is frozen,

17
00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:09.020
and the AI still offered two hundred and seventy dollars.

18
00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:13.240
The check caught it, so there's no send button.

19
00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:15.690
Only a person can answer.

20
00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:20.890
Every AI letter has to pass ten written rules,

21
00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:26.320
and an admin can make the checks stricter or softer, live.

22
00:01:26.370 --> 00:01:30.350
The AI earns more freedom only with results:

23
00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:35.320
auto-send stays off until it proves itself on real mail.

24
00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:39.640
Then every bought link is watched:

25
00:01:39.690 --> 00:01:44.010
is it still there, still dofollow, still indexed?

26
00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:46.480
A lost link becomes a ticket,

27
00:01:46.530 --> 00:01:49.190
then a letter asking for it back —

28
00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:51.670
but only after a second check,

29
00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:56.090
because almost one dead link in five was actually alive.

30
00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:02.570
Around it: payment requests, three user roles,

31
00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:07.170
spend meters and alerts before a balance runs out.

32
00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:09.910
More than eleven thousand automated

33
00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:12.240
tests keep it all working.

34
00:02:13.970 --> 00:02:16.910
I build systems like this fast.

35
00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:20.050
My latest outreach service went live

36
00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:23.660
for an SEO agency in eight days.
